[36m(RolloutManager pid=1913)[0m [2026-09-29 06:15:19.223 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:473 - First rollout sample: ['<|im_start|>user\nArnel had ten boxes of pencils with the same number of pencils in each box.  He kept ten pencils and shared the remaining pencils equally with his five friends. If his friends got eight pencils each, how many pencils are in each box?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nWe are told:\n\n- Arnel has **10 boxes** of pencils, and each has the same number of pencils.\n- He keeps **ten pencils**, so the **remaining pencils (10 boxes × pencils per box) – 10 = 90 pencils** are shared equally among his **five friends**, and they **each got 8 pencils**.\n\n### Step 1: Let the number of pencils in each box be $ x $\n\nSo:\n- Total pencils = $ 10x $ (since there are 10 boxes)\n- He keeps 10, so the remaining total is $ 10x - 10 $\n- He shares this among 5 friends, so each friend gets:\n  $$\n  \\frac{10x - 10}{5} = 8\n  $$\n\n### Step 2: Solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{10x - 10}{5} = 8\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by 5:\n\n$$\n10x - 10 = 40\n$$\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n$$\n10x = 50\n$$\n\nDivide by 10:\n\n$$\nx = 5\n$$\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{5}\n$$\n\nThere are **5 pencils in each box**.<|im_end|>'], label: 5, reward: 1.0
